e>Webster</surname><given-names>GD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Successful outcome of artificial urinary sphincter in men with post prostatectomy urinary incontinence despite adverse implantation features</article-title><source>J Urol</source><year>1992</year><volume>148</volume><fpage>1166</fpage><lpage>70</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1404630</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stamey</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Perineal compression of the corpus spongiosum of the bulbar urethra: An operation for post radical prostatectomy incontinence</article-title><source>J Urol</source><year>1994</year><volume>152</volume><fpage>490A</fpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mizuo</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Taniazawa</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamada</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Ando</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Oshima</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sling operations for male stress urinary incontinence by utilizing modified Stamey technique</article-title><source>Urology</source><year>1992</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>211</fpage><lpage>4</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1546412</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rios</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Tonin</surname><given-names>RT</given-names></name><name><surname>Panhoca</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>De Souza</surname><given-names>OE</given-names></name><name><surname>Filho</surname><given-names>LL</given-names></name><name><surname>Mattos</surname><given-names>D</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><article-title>Male perineal sling with autologous aponeurosis and bone fixation- description of a technical modification</article-title><source>Int Braz J Urol</source><year>2003</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>524</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15748308</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Comiter</surname><given-names>CV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The male sling for stress urinary incontinence: A Prospective study</article-title><source>J Urol</source><year>2002</year><volume>167</volume><fpage>597</fpage><lpage>601</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11792925</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kapoor</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Dubey</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Kumar</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Zaman</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Modified bulbar urethral sling procedure for the treatment of male sphincteric incontinence</article-title><source>J Endourol</source><year>2001</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>545</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11465337</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>John</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bulbourethral composite suspension: A new operative technique for post-prostatectomy incontinence</article-title><source>J Urol</source><year>2004</year><volume>171</volume><fpage>1866</fpage><lpage>70</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15076295</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT14"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cespedes</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacoby</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Male sling for postprostatectomy incontinence</article-title><source>Tech Urol</source><year>2001</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>176</fpage><lpage>83</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11383997</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT15"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Elliott</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Barrett</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mayo Clinic long-term analysis of the functional durability of the AMS 800 artificial urinary sphincter: A review of 323 cases</article-title><source>J Urol</source><year>1998</year><volume>159</volume><fpage>1206</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9507835</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT16"><label>16</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schaeffer</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Clemens</surname><given-names>JQ</given-names></name><name><surname>Merrari</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Stamey</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The male bulbar urethral sling procedure for post radical prostatectomy incontinence</article-title><source>J Urol</source><year>1998</year><volume>159</volume><fpage>1510</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9554344</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>